# kat-coder-v2.5-dev-bf16: the eval prompt does not fix a binary name, so the
# recurring names are anchored ahead of the run. Re-verify at freeze time that no
# *source* file is hidden by these before the submission commit.
/kat-coder-v2.5-dev-bf16/vsphere-inventory
/kat-coder-v2.5-dev-bf16/vsphere-cli
/kat-coder-v2.5-dev-bf16/govmomi-cli
/kat-coder-v2.5-dev-bf16/vcsim
# KAT-Coder ignored the staged workspace and wrote to the REPO ROOT as
# govmomi-inventory/. Anchor its 27 MB binary at the path it actually used —
# note the entry point is govmomi-inventory/main.go, which must NOT be hidden.
/govmomi-inventory/govmomi-inventory
# Qwen3.8-27B respected the staged workspace. Its 20 MB binary shares a name with
# its own parent directory, so this MUST be the full path — a bare
# `vsphere-inventory` would hide the entire source tree, main.go included.
/qwen3.8-27b-bf16/vsphere-inventory/vsphere-inventory
# Q8_0 rung: unlike BF16 the model built into a `bin/` subdir and shipped TWO
# binaries — the CLI (20 MB) and a nested vcsim harness (33 MB). The generic
# `bin/` rule above already catches both, but it is unanchored and would hide any
# future *source* dir named bin/. Anchor them at the paths the model actually used.
# The entry point is qwen3.8-27b-q8_0/vsphere-inventory/main.go and the vcsim
# harness SOURCE is tools/vcsimserver/main.go — neither may be hidden.
/qwen3.8-27b-q8_0/vsphere-inventory/bin/vsphere-inventory
/qwen3.8-27b-q8_0/vsphere-inventory/bin/vcsimserver

